{"operations":[{"content":"\"\"\"luhn: Luhn checksum validation for identification numbers.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef is_valid(text):\n    digits = [int(ch) for ch in text if ch.isdigit()]\n    if len(digits) < 2:\n        return False\n    total = 0\n    # Double every second digit from the right (excluding the check digit at the rightmost)\n    for i in range(len(digits)):\n        digit = digits[-(i + 1)]\n        if i % 2 == 1:\n            digit *= 2\n            if digit > 9:\n                digit -= 9\n        total += digit\n    return total % 10 == 0\n","expected_sha256":"daa56df7794aa8b4da213da4d9fdee84518147a03a7f4ee745a11a06b101c3b1","kind":"modify","path":"src/luhn.py"}],"rationale":"Fixed the doubling logic to correctly double every second digit from the right, excluding the rightmost check digit, as per the Luhn algorithm specification."}